From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx: iceland: keep CLX off unless msm.enable_clx=1

Since commit 08d5049d9e84 ("drm/msm/a6xx: Enable CLX feature on A840")
the GMU gets the A840 CLX and IFF/PCLX tables at every HFI start. On the
OnePlus Pad 4 (SM8850, A840, msm built in) the GMU then times out on
GX_BW_PERF_VOTE and the GPU does not come up, with every GMU firmware, TZ
request and CX GDSC variant tried. The likely root cause is rpmhpd
clamping gfx / gmxc before sync_state, which the rpmhpd fix now in this
tree addresses, but that has not been proven on the hardware yet.

Keep the upstream tables and add a module parameter instead of the
earlier revert: CLX stays off by default (the device owner's rule until a
test boot proves it), msm.enable_clx=1 turns it on for a test boot. Off
is the same path as a GPU without a CLX table. One line in the kernel
log says which way it went.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_hfi.c      | 13 +++++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c |  4 ++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.h    |  1 +
 3 files changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_hfi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_hfi.c
index 6b34e704a70d..1ab46097c2c3 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_hfi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_hfi.c
@@ -938,6 +938,19 @@ static int a6xx_hfi_enable_clx(struct a6xx_gmu *gmu)
 	if (!info->clx_tbl)
 		return 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * Off unless msm.enable_clx=1: with this kernel's built-in msm the GMU
+	 * times out on GX_BW_PERF_VOTE during the CLX sequence on A840 and the
+	 * GPU does not start (fixed by rpmhpd not clamping gfx / gmxc before
+	 * sync_state, to be proven on the hardware before CLX is turned on).
+	 */
+	if (!enable_clx) {
+		DRM_DEV_INFO_ONCE(gmu->dev, "CLX table present, CLX off (msm.enable_clx=0)\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
+
+	DRM_DEV_INFO_ONCE(gmu->dev, "CLX on (msm.enable_clx=1)\n");
+
 	ret = a6xx_hfi_feature_ctrl_msg(gmu, HFI_FEATURE_CLX, 1, 0);
 	if (ret) {
 		DRM_DEV_ERROR(gmu->dev, "Unable to enable CLX (%d)\n", ret);
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
index 2ec130c1cf71..4699f2a93a2c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
@@ -28,6 +28,10 @@ bool disable_acd;
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(disable_acd, "Forcefully disable GPU ACD");
 module_param_unsafe(disable_acd, bool, 0400);
 
+bool enable_clx;
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(enable_clx, "Enable the GPU current limiter (CLX) on GPUs with a CLX table (0=off (default), 1=on)");
+module_param(enable_clx, bool, 0400);
+
 static bool skip_gpu;
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(skip_gpu, "Disable GPU driver register (0=enable GPU driver register (default), 1=skip GPU driver register");
 module_param(skip_gpu, bool, 0400);
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.h
index 4b2156825bdf..06c7899f414c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.h
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include "adreno_pm4.xml.h"
 
 extern bool snapshot_debugbus;
+extern bool enable_clx;
 
 enum {
 	ADRENO_FW_PM4 = 0,
